  "generated_text": "1. Given \\( g(x) = \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x+3}{4}} \\), we need to solve \\( g(2x) = 2(g(x)) \\).\n\n2. First, express \\( g(2x) \\) and \\( g(x) \\) in terms of \\( x \\):\n   - \\( g(2x) = \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{2x+3}{4}} \\)\n   - \\( g(x) = \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x+3}{4}} \\)\n\n3. Set \\( g(2x) = 2(g(x)) \\):\n   - \\( \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{2x+3}{4}} = 2\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{x+3}{4}} \\)\n\n4. Cube both sides to eliminate the cube roots:\n   - \\( \\frac{2x+3}{4} = 8 \\cdot \\frac{x+3}{4} \\)\n\n5. Simplify the equation:\n   - \\( 2x = 8x \\)\n\n6. Solve for \\( x \\):\n   - \\( x = 0 \\)\n\n\\(\\boxed{0}\\)",
